ubisoft is ending support for ghost  recon break point ubisoft might have a  new battle royale and lara croft is  ending her vacation  the day has come ghost recon breakpoint  will no longer be supported ubisoft made  the announcement in a twitter update and  said quote the last four months have  marked the release of our final piece of  content but don't mourn the game just  yet you can get in plenty of playtime  still ubisoft said it will continue to  maintain the servers for both wildlands  and break point until further notice  over the last several months ghost recon  breakpoint content began winding down  with the launch of operation mother lode  mode anniversary content that celebrated  the 20th anniversary of the series in  2021 and the controversial quartz nfts  that received a lot of consumer backlash  as for the future of the franchise ghost  recon frontline will carry the brand  forward it's a first-person battle  royale focused multiplayer entry into  the series that focuses on teams of  players battling it out to find crucial  intel and extract them from the  battlefield before it's too late but  that isn't yubi's only battle royale in  the works a new report states that a new  third-person hero shooter take on the  genre tentatively titled pathfinder is  reportedly in early stages of  development at ubisoft montreal the  report comes from tom henderson who says  he's seen images and videos of the game  in action and it looks similar to  ubisoft's almost dead battle royale  hyperscape but more cartoony in nature  pathfinder is said to be a pvpve take on  battle royale with players having to  battle both ai enemies and other  competitors as they work their way  towards the center of the map to defeat  a boss-like enemy to reach the boss in  the center players will need to breach  an outer and inner wall via a series of  gates that change on a per-match basis  henderson reports that the game will be  a hero shooter in that there will be  different playable characters to choose  from that each have their own unique  abilities pathfinder will also  reportedly have a destiny-like social  space where players can shop test out  weapons at a firing range join events  and interact with other players  pathfinder is coming from the same  studio that made hyperscape which is set  to shut down on april 28th personally i  think ubisoft should slow down with  these shooters the company said it would  learn from the mistakes of hyperscape  but pumping out frontline pathfinder and  ex-defiance soonish seems like they're  just throwing games at the wall praying  one sticks long enough to be a  competitor for warzone fortnite or  overwatch let me know in the comments if  you think i'm way off base with that  tape but in some non-ubisoft news laura  croft saw the uncharted movie and  thought you've gone too far nate my  hiatus is over during epic's state of  unreal event crystal dynamics confirmed  that it has begun work on the next tomb  raider game and that it will run on  unreal engine 5. the studio added quote  our goal is to push the envelope of  fidelity and to deliver the high quality  cinematic action adventure experience  that fans deserve from both crystal  dynamics and the tomb raider franchise  this will be the first new entry in the  series since 2018's shadow of the tomb  raider which was developed by idah's  montreal and wrapped up the events of  the new trilogy that started in 2015. i  fell off the new trilogy and never got  around to playing shadow but my wife is  a huge fan of all three and immediately  wanted a release date for this new one  when i told her it was announced so  congrats tomb raider fans i'm sure this  game is gonna be sick however if it  comes out around the same time as the  new witcher i'm gonna have to toss it on  the backlog cause monster slang comes  first  i'll see you tomorrow  you
 

